00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.692
This lesson becomes clearer when before the worked example, treat capacitance as charge stored per volt instead of as a pile of charge by itself.

2
00:00:05.692 --> 00:00:11.384
Stored quantity means charge: Charge is what accumulates on the capacitor plates.

3
00:00:11.384 --> 00:00:17.075
Storage ratio means capacitance: Capacitance tells how much charge is stored for each volt across the capacitor.

4
00:00:17.075 --> 00:00:22.767
Main trap means treating C as Q: Capacitance is not the stored charge.

5
00:00:22.767 --> 00:00:28.459
It is the link between charge and p.d.

6
00:00:28.459 --> 00:00:34.151
Capacitance is the storage ratio Q per V, not the charge itself.

